WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.035
Back from a shoot with hundreds of frames?

00:00:03.035 --> 00:00:05.760
LumiRaw's cull page helps you find the keepers.

00:00:06.061 --> 00:00:07.618
Drop in the whole folder.

00:00:07.618 --> 00:00:12.788
Every photo is scored, right in your browser, for how it looks and how sharp it is.

00:00:12.788 --> 00:00:16.525
It reads the preview the camera stored inside each raw file,

00:00:16.525 --> 00:00:18.331
so even a big shoot is quick.

00:00:18.732 --> 00:00:22.995
Near-identical shots, like a burst or a bracket, are grouped together,

00:00:22.995 --> 00:00:25.552
and only the best of each group is picked.

00:00:25.552 --> 00:00:29.632
Blown highlights and crushed shadows are flagged under every photo.

00:00:30.036 --> 00:00:31.742
You decide what counts more:

00:00:31.742 --> 00:00:34.606
a sharp, clean frame, or how the picture looks.

00:00:34.606 --> 00:00:38.506
And how many to keep, as a number, or a percentage of the shoot.

00:00:42.429 --> 00:00:45.235
Click any photo to pick it, or to leave it out.

00:00:45.235 --> 00:00:46.549
Your call always wins.

00:00:46.948 --> 00:00:49.976
When you're happy, send the picks straight to the developer,

00:00:49.976 --> 00:00:51.238
lined up and ready to go.
